'' Linux is 64-bit only by decision: x86-32 Linux is a third set of layout numbers
'' (wchar is 4 bytes there) and nobody has asked for it. The refusal must be a clear
'' error rather than a silently ignored flag, in EITHER argument order.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -m32 -target linux-x86_64 tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: FBX0104: 32-bit is supported on Windows only
